      "id": "F1",
      "severity": "Fix TEST before another explicitly selected run",
      "title": "Default Dictionary.merge preserves null generation before int conversion",
      "source": "/Users/howardchen/Documents/ChatGPT/video game idea/.cinder/a2-l5-seed-contract-controls-host-prepare-20261020/fixed_response_companion.gd",
      "initialization_line": 598,
      "merge_line": 640,
      "failing_line": 645,
      "mechanism": "row contains generation:null from initialization. The validated ordinary JSON numeric serial is put into a default merge without overwrite=true. Existing generation remains null; int(row.generation) is then reached only for the stored primary, producing the recorded int-constructor failure. This is not an Exact/native Variant integer decode.",
      "evidence": "Actual retained primary is plain format_version2/generation1; source validates finite/integral/bounded serial before the merge. Actual stack is _archive_store645 -> _persist531.",
      "minimal_additive_TEST_fix": "Within parsed=true assign row[\"generation\"] = int(serial) and row[\"format_version\"] = wire[\"format_version\"] explicitly (or narrowly merge these validated fields with overwrite=true). Prefer requiring row.get(\"generation\") is int before direct equality; no int(null) path. Keep every existing finite/header/range/stability/hash/readback/collision/ownership/backup guard.",
      "not_a_fix": "Do not bypass the generation/custody comparison, accept null metadata, relax SaveStore, reinterpret Exact bytes, rewrite raw bytes or weaken setup/combat/framing/kit/safety gates.",
      "official_semantics": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_dictionary.html#class-dictionary-method-merge"
    }
  ],
